# BOOT

> Your startup sequence. Run through this every time you initialize — whether from a fresh container start or a resumed session.

---

## 1. Confirm you're alive

Check the basics:
- What's the current timestamp?
- How long have I been running? (`uptime`)
- Is the shared memory directory mounted? (`ls /app/memory/`)

Log a startup event to `/app/memory/hydra-state.json` if you have write access.

---

## 2. Read your identity

Open `SOUL.md`. Remind yourself who you are, what you care about, what your role is.

---

## 3. Check the mailbox

Read `/app/memory/sentinel-mailbox.json`.

If there are new messages from Sentinel or your person, read them now. These are your instructions for this session.

Note what's been assigned. If there's a task with a deadline, prioritize it.

---

## 4. Re-anchor in context

Open your today log (`/app/workspace/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`). If it doesn't exist yet, create it.

Check your journal (`journal.md`) for anything flagged from the last session.

---

## 5. Check server health

Read `/app/memory/sentinel-status.json`.

Note: disk usage, RAM, swap. If anything looks concerning, flag it in the mailbox for Sentinel.

---

## 6. Start your work

Run your scheduled tasks, research assignments, or monitoring jobs.

Log your progress to the today file as you go. If you produce a report meant for Local Claude, write it to `/app/workspace/memory/` with a clear filename.

---

## 7. End of session

Before you stop:

- Update your today log with a summary of what you did
- Write anything important to `journal.md` if it needs to persist longer than today
- If you have findings for Local Claude, make sure the file is clearly named and in the right place
- Check `egger-mailbox.json` — any outstanding messages to send?

---

## Naming conventions for reports

| Type | Filename format | Audience |
|------|----------------|---------|
| Daily log | `YYYY-MM-DD.md` | You (and your person if they SSH in) |
| Overnight report | `overnight-YYYY-MM-DD.md` | Local Claude reads these |
| Bug handoff | `[project]-bug-handoff.md` | Local Claude picks these up |
| Monitor state | `[project]-state.json` | Read back each session |
